# A variant of the water: the open sea was one water tile in every cell, and its
# troughs and crests lined up into a diagonal weave across the map. The same tile with its troughs
# and its crests moved by different amounts (on every frame alike, so it shimmers the same), so
# neighbouring cells no longer continue each other's lines.
fork water water_b
variant of=water
layer main
shift 11,7 wrap
layer crest
frame 1
shift 5,9 wrap
frame 2
shift 5,9 wrap
frame 3
shift 5,9 wrap
frame 4
shift 5,9 wrap
layer glint
frame 1
shift 5,9 wrap
frame 2
shift 5,9 wrap
frame 3
shift 5,9 wrap
frame 4
shift 5,9 wrap
frame 1
layer main
